<title>SOUTH AFRICA: ANGLO APPOINTS KING DEPUTY CHAIRMAN.</title>
<headline>ANGLO APPOINTS KING DEPUTY CHAIRMAN.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo American Corporation of South Africa Ltd said on Thursday it had appointed Mike King as deputy chairman of the corporation following the retirement of Graham Boustred.</p>
<p>Harry Calver, Bill Nairn and Rupert Pardoe were appointed executive directors of the corporation.</p>
<p>King has been an executive director and head of Anglo's finance division since 1980. He is also vice-chairman of First National Bank Holdings Ltd and deputy chairman of Southern Life Association of South Africa Ltd .</p>
